<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 4.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<!--
  The fixture the engraving-polish change is checked against, written by hand
  for the score view's `score-view-engraving` capture surface.

  Every bar holds one thing that change has to get right, and it was captured
  *before* any of them was fixed, so each tier has a picture to compare with:

    bar 1   a C-sharp major triad with a sharp on every note (two columns of
            accidentals), then a second under an up stem with the sharp on the
            upper, shifted note
    bar 2   two seconds under down stems: one with the sharp on the note that
            stays, one with the sharp on the lower note, the one that moves left
    bar 3   a Segno, and lyrics under notes with ledger lines below the staff
    bars 4-5  a tie from the last note of bar 4 to the first of bar 5, which is
            where the first system breaks at the docked view's width
    bar 6   a forward repeat
    bar 7   a first ending, closed by a backward repeat
    bar 8   a second ending, left open
    bars 9-12  four bars of rest in a row
    bar 13  "D.S. al Coda" and the final barline

  Hand-written for this repository, like everything else in this directory, and
  made only of elements the importer recognises, so it imports with no
  diagnostics and the picture is of the renderer rather than of a report.

  **The Segno and "D.S. al Coda" are read and dropped by the importer today,
  without a diagnostic.** `<segno>` is a known element that nothing reads, and
  `<words>` is kept only as a tempo mark's text, so neither reaches
  `RepeatMarkings::jumps` -- which nothing fills. They are here because the
  fixture is meant to hold them once tasks 1.14 and its importer half land;
  until then the picture shows bar 3 and bar 13 without them, and
  ApprovedScoreFixturesTests pins that gap rather than hiding it.

  No dynamic, for the reason notation-sample.musicxml gives.

  Divisions are 4, so a quarter note is 4 and a bar of 4/4 is 16.
-->
<score-partwise version="4.0">
  <work>
    <work-title>Engraving Polish</work-title>
  </work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">Practice Takes</creator>
